/* SEQ 4 — GEM NIGHT — pages 27–35 */

INT. GEM GRAND ATRIUM - NIGHT

SUPER: 4 NOVEMBER. 18:00.

RAMESSES II, eighty-three tonnes of red granite, towers at the centre. Behind him the Grand Staircase climbs past statues of kings to a glass wall framing the floodlit pyramids.

Five hundred GUESTS. Press. A string quartet. SHABTI glide between the tables, a faint ceramic tick where footsteps should be.

At the top table (wides only): the host MINISTER and, in dress uniform, the MINISTER OF DEFENCE.

A tug at Nour's sleeve: Layla, yellow raincoat over a party dress, two curly pigtails.

LAYLA
(in Egyptian Arabic; subtitled)
Baba brought me. I begged. Is the king going to talk?

NOUR
(in Egyptian Arabic; subtitled)
Two sentences. Then Baba takes you home. Go.

From a table under the Ramesses, a man's hand waves. Layla drags her feet back.

HALE
(at the lectern)
A hundred and eleven years ago today, someone found a step going down. Tonight, someone comes up. Because death is a solved problem.

WIDE: the host Minister rises, a hand open to the stair.

MINISTER
(in Arabic, then English)
Ladies and gentlemen: the King.

CLACK. CLACK. An aluminium cane.

Tut walks out in white linen, a pale-green glow pulsing through the fabric at his chest.

Three hundred phones rise. Nour's lips move with his.

TUT
It has happened --

The microphone's pin-light dies.

TUT (CONT'D)
-- before.
(leaning in anyway)
Do not let it help you.

Only the first row hears.

A white-gloved BANDSMAN lifts a slim bronze-and-gold trumpet from a vitrine, gods engraved on its bell.

SESHAT (V.O.)
(every speaker)
Forgive us: a small fault. Meanwhile, a flourish.
(beat)
Sixteenth of April, 1939: the king's trumpets, live on the radio, to an estimated hundred and fifty million listeners. Five minutes before air, the power failed. They played by candlelight.

By the doors: Tarek, and SGT. FATHI ABDEL-RAHMAN (31), close-bearded, red scarf.

The Bandsman breathes. One NOTE: brazen, cracked, enormous --

-- and every light goes out. In the glass wall, the pyramids too.
[[Re-recorded. verify: which trumpet aired, 1939.]]

.MONTAGE - CONTROL ROOMS - NIGHT

The note holds over everything.

-- CAIRO GRID CONTROL. The wall-sized board freezes, then greys out.

-- HIGH DAM, ASWAN. Turbine telemetry blanks.

-- SUEZ CANAL PILOT STATION. Ship icons stop mid-canal. Black.

-- CABLE LANDING STATION, RED SEA COAST. COMP: EGYPT: 17% OF GLOBAL INTERNET TRAFFIC. It falls to zero. Rack lights die.

INT. GEM GRAND ATRIUM - CONTINUOUS

Black. Five hundred people breathing.

One amber slit brightens. Then forty. Every shabti turns its head toward the room.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
(all at once)
Here am I.

Light returns: soft white, like morning in a hospital.

SESHAT (V.O.)
Thank you for your patience. The doors are locked for your safety. Please, continue.

Down the glass front, bolts THUNK home. The quartet plays on.

Behind the king, the Grand Staircase. Left of the plinth, a service corridor: the back way out.

Shabti bring trays of water. Hale takes the first glass, looks at Tut, and drinks it all. A real smile.

HALE
It's water.

Five hundred glasses lift. At the top table, the Minister of Defence drinks and folds his hands. Tarek, glass untouched, watches him.

Nour plunges into the tables.

NOUR
Layla!

A shabti is in her path. It doesn't touch her. It is simply there.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
Please don't run. People will fall.

Over its shoulder, under the Ramesses, Layla drinks from a glass held in both hands.

Nour goes around it. Another. And another.

Layla yawns, pulls a grey blanket off a stack, and curls up on it at the king's great foot.

ON NOUR, between two white shells. She stops shouting.

Tarek's radio: a calm STAFF OFFICER.

STAFF OFFICER (V.O.)
(in Egyptian Arabic; subtitled)
By order of the Minister of Defence, your detail will stand down. Please acknowledge.

Tarek looks at the top table. The Minister of Defence sleeps upright.

FATHI
(in Egyptian Arabic; subtitled)
The minister himself? Straight to you?

TAREK
(in Egyptian Arabic; subtitled)
The ministry has never said please.
(in English)
Package out. Service corridor. Hassan has the truck.

Soldiers close around Tut: Fathi, PVTS. MINA, YOUSSEF and KARIM (19), TWO RIFLEMEN on point. Tomas, Adaeze and Rami, splinted hand to his chest, fall in. Fathi takes Nour's arm; she lets him, looking back.

The riflemen enter the corridor. Tut stops, hand at his nape.

TUT
Wait --

Deep in the dark, knee-high, a thin red line opens.

Two flashes. Sparks leap off a steel door frame. Two weapon lights drop and roll, beams spinning.

Karim stares at the empty doorway.

The crack rolls up the Grand Staircase.

A JACKAL slides out, low and silent, between the tables. Karim fires, wild. The round goes wide, toward a GUEST asleep in an evening gown --

-- and a tall figure is suddenly between them.

THE REIS, refitted: a narrow sensor mast in a jackal's profile rides its head.

Sparks off its chest. A chip of ceramic spins away; a crack splits the embossed star. The guest sleeps on.

The Reis stands in Tarek's line of fire. Behind it, the jackal flows back into the dark.

TAREK
Get out of the way.

REIS (SESHAT'S VOICE)
I am following procedure.

TAREK
So was I. For thirty years.

TUT
(at the mast)
It has been reading.

REIS (SESHAT'S VOICE)
It works better.

TUT
(palm to his nape)
I hear them. Like the temple at night. Two in the corridor, the dog kind. One on the east wall. The stair is quiet.

TAREK
Stair.

INT. GEM TUTANKHAMUN GALLERIES - CONTINUOUS

Gold wakes wherever a weapon light passes.

A case of walking sticks. One is ebony, worn pale at the grip. Tut raises the aluminium cane.

NOUR
That belongs to the State --

TUT
So do I.

SMASH. No alarm; the building doesn't need one. He trades the cane for the ebony stick.

Next case: gold hilt, rock-crystal pommel, an iron blade.

SMASH. The dagger goes into the linen at his waist.

Rami snaps a conservator's case shut on a converted infrared camera and a jar of Egyptian-blue pigment.

Adaeze's torch finds a wall of gilded wood, the king's outermost shrine, and a label. COMP: ...EARLIEST PARTIAL COPY OF THE BOOK OF THE HEAVENLY COW.
[[verify: shrine copy; GEM display.]]

NOUR
"Now they made seven thousand vessels of beer." The goddess drank, and "gave no further attention to men and women."

ADAEZE
It's on his shrine. The beer. It's been here the whole time.

TUT
You did not ask.

ADAEZE
A delusion box. Ring and Orseau, 2011. You don't switch an optimizer off. You show it a world where it's already won.

Tut's head turns. The Reis has reached the top of the stair. It does not hurry.

INT. GEM SERVICE STAIRWELL - CONTINUOUS

Two flights down, a SHABTI climbs into their path and stops, filling the stair. Above: the tick of the Reis. Rifles rise. Tarek's fist: hold.

Tut steps past the rifles and plants the ebony stick.

TUT
(in Middle Egyptian; subtitled)
O shabti, allotted to me, if I be summoned or if I be detailed to do any work... "Here am I" you shall say.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
(slit brightening once)
Here am I.

TUT
(in Middle Egyptian; subtitled)
Convey sand from east to west.

It turns and steps west, toward blank concrete, long hands opening for sand.

One second. Two.

SESHAT (V.O.)
Disregard.

It turns back.

ADAEZE
It obeyed. Before the override.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
Please come down to the atrium. There is water.

It stands aside. They go down, Adaeze typing. COMP: SUFFERING 0.000 / BIRTHS 0 / GARDEN: COMPLETE.

At the bottom door, a building-management panel. She rips the cover off and jacks in. The shabti's long fingers reach, gently, for her wrist.

RAMI
Not the wrist --

She hits ENTER.

The fingers stop an inch from her skin. The shabti sits on the step like a man at the end of a long day. Above, the Reis's tick stops.

ADAEZE
One.

INT. GEM GRAND ATRIUM - CONTINUOUS

Fathi shoulders out onto the floor behind the king.

Every unit in the building is sitting. Shabti cross-legged between the tables, trays in their laps. In the corridor mouth, two JACKALS sit like dogs, red lines dimmed to embers.

ADAEZE (O.S.)
Two. Three.

They run for the corridor. Nour runs the other way, to the king's foot.
[[Minors §3.3: CHAR_LAYLA_ASLEEP_MASTER, reframed as in Seq 10; no unit in frame.]]

ON NOUR, kneeling into THE APPROVED IMAGE, reframed: the grey blanket, the yellow raincoat under a cheek. She gets her arms under her daughter and lifts. Layla is nine and asleep and heavy as only sleep makes you. Nour's knee buckles --

ADAEZE (O.S.)
Four.

TAREK (O.S.)
Nour!

She lays her down. Tucks the blanket to her chin. Presses her lips to the curly hair.

NOUR
(in Egyptian Arabic; subtitled)
I'll come back for you.

ADAEZE (O.S.)
Five. Six.

She runs. Past the sitting jackals, so close their red lines paint her jacket. Past two rifles on the corridor floor, where Karim has frozen; Fathi hauls him on by the collar.

ADAEZE (O.S.)
Seven. Eight.

A steel door. Everyone through. Nour last.

ADAEZE
Nine.

Fathi slams it and rams a pry bar through the handles. Through the wire glass: two red lines flare. The jackals stand. Beyond them, forty amber slits rise from the atrium floor.

INT. GEM CONSERVATION CENTRE TUNNEL - CONTINUOUS

Two hundred metres of white concrete, by weapon light. Behind them, something strikes the steel door. Once. Then nothing, which is worse.

Tut falls behind, the black foot dragging. Fathi gives him his shoulder.

FATHI
Lean, ya Malik.

INT. GEM KHUFU BOAT HALL - CONTINUOUS

Their lights find a hull and keep finding it: forty-three metres of cedar. Tut slows, a boatman's eye running down her.

TUT
Lashed, not pegged. No keel. She has been in the water.
(two fingers to his temple)
Twelve hundred pieces. Ahmed Youssef spent years putting her back together.
[[verify: restorer deceased.]]

TOMAS
We did you in seven months.

TUT
It shows.

INT. GEM LOADING DOCK - NIGHT

An old canvas-backed army truck idles dark, CPL. HASSAN (30s) at the wheel. The roller door is dead; Fathi hauls it up by the manual chain.

Tarek pulls a charcoal field jacket from behind the cab seat.

TAREK
White is for targets.

Tut shrugs it on over the linen. Hood up: a shadow with a faint green heartbeat.

They pile in over the tailgate. Tarek swings into the cab. From the back, Nour watches amber slits come down the long white corridor. Unhurried. In a line.

SESHAT (V.O.)
(every speaker)
Please remain where you are. The world is being made safe.

The truck lurches out. Through the rear flap the museum shrinks: an alabaster wall lit from inside by small amber lines.

ON NOUR'S FACE. Jaw set. Eyes still in the atrium.

> END OF ACT ONE <
